@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to Customer Account Employee Permissions
	Testing to assure that customer account employee permissions work properly.

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate past static start and end dates
	* I generate future static start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                         |
	| Group         | Employees                         |
	| Group         | Account Access US                 |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.employee2                    |
	| Email Address | cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee2                         |
	| Group         | Employees                         |
	| Group         | Account Access EU                 |
    * I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | KORCSTKORCST                  | |
	| Name   | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | KORCT2KORCT2                   | |
	| Name   | Korcst2 - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | Spain                          | |
	| Status | Active                         | |
	| Tier   | T1                             | |

Teardown:
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| CSTM Customer |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	| KORCT2KORCT2 |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korcst - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Korcst2 - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	| KORCT2KORCT2 |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| cstm.employee2@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: View US and EU Region accounts as an US Employee on Customer
	New Liferay US employees added via okta should be able to view US and EU Region accounts on Customer

	Guiven I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And the support user with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
    And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access US"
	Then the team with the name "Account Access US" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access US"
	When I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"
	Then I should be able to view the following project "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" values in the customer project details page
	| Name           | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | KORCSTKORCST                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| SLA            | -                             |
	| Support Seats  | 0 / 0 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T1                            |
	| FLS Partner    | -                             |
	And I should be able to view the following project "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" values in the customer project details page
	| Name           | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | KORCSTKORCST                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | Spain                         |
	| SLA            | -                             |
	| Support Seats  | 0 / 0 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T1                            |
	| FLS Partner    | -                             |

Scenario: View EU Region account as an EU Employee on Customer
	New Liferay EU employees added via okta should be able to view EU Region accounts on Customer

	Given I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And the support user with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "cstm.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
    And I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access US"
	Then the team with the name "Account Access US" should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access US"
	When I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"
	Then I should be able to view the following project "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" values in the customer project details page
	| Name           | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | KORCSTKORCST                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| SLA            | -                             |
	| Support Seats  | 0 / 0 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T1                            |
	| FLS Partner    | -                             |
	And I should be able to view the following project "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" values in the customer project details page
	| Name           | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | KORCSTKORCST                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | Spain                         |
	| SLA            | -                             |
	| Support Seats  | 0 / 0 Filled                  |
	| Tier           | T1                            |
	| FLS Partner    | -                             |